fix(engine): report the live committed permission on a shared row

Engine::received_shares filled ReceivedShareRow.permission from the
durable bookmark, which holds the accept-time copy. The accept flow is
the one writer of that field, so an owner downgrade from write to read
never reached the /shared row without a re-accept.

The row now reads the permission from the received-verdict map, the same
map the resolution field reads, and falls back to the bookmark copy
until a pass resolves the share. The render permission map already
honoured a downgrade, so the two surfaces now agree.

The new engine unit test an_owner_downgrade_reaches_the_shared_row_permission
accepts a write grant, serves a demoted scope root at a higher sequence,
runs the passes that clear the /shared damper, and asserts the row turns
to read while the standing stays granted. The test fails on the previous
code at the read assertion.

The staging spec writable-share.spec.ts asserted the permission once,
under the Playwright default of 5 seconds, because the standing is
granted both before and after a downgrade. It now polls the row
permission through the new SharedPage.awaitPermission helper, which
nudges the sync pass each turn.

Closes #1925.

